+Period contract
+---------------
+Scheduled run due at 03:00 UTC on date D  ->  processes calendar day D-1 (UTC).
+  ``data_interval_start`` = D-1 00:00 UTC, ``data_interval_end`` = D 00:00 UTC.
+Backfill for tick D                        ->  same interval as the scheduled run for D.
+Rerun / clear of any run                   ->  same ``data_interval_start``, same day;
+  the DELETE-then-INSERT transaction makes every rerun produce identical rows.
+Manual trigger                             ->  ``run_window()`` falls back to
+  ``(logical_date or run_after) - 1 day`` so the helper always returns a day.
+
+Backfill behaviour
+------------------
+``catchup=True`` + ``start_date=2026-09-01 03:00 UTC`` means that when the DAG
+is unpaused the scheduler will create one run per day from that first tick up to
+the current time, filling all of September automatically.  ``max_active_runs=1``
+prevents concurrent writers on the single DuckDB file.
 """
 
